WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.262
Welcome to the Portfolio Tracker dashboard.

2
00:00:03.262 --> 00:00:12.929
This is the day-to-day command center for the account: performance, income, risk, allocation, upcoming payments, and holding-level detail on one page.

3
00:00:12.929 --> 00:00:28.120
In this walkthrough, we will examine the entire dashboard, explain what every group of boxes is showing, and work through the chart controls, date ranges, calendar, category drilldowns, and all four table views.

4
00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:36.022
At the top, the page identifies the active account and the number of holdings included.

5
00:00:36.022 --> 00:00:41.830
Portfolio Value is the full account today: open holdings plus any idle cash.

6
00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:50.320
Account Change is the move from the previous market close to the latest observation, with both dollars and percent.

7
00:00:50.320 --> 00:01:01.936
Tracker Price Return measures price performance for every position held at any time in the selected range, including positions that were completely sold during that window.

8
00:01:01.936 --> 00:01:07.298
Open Lots Price Return narrows the calculation to positions still owned now.

9
00:01:07.298 --> 00:01:12.660
Open Lots Total Return uses that same open-position scope, then adds distributions.

10
00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:19.362
Tracker Total Return adds distributions to the broader tracker history, including qualifying fully closed positions.

11
00:01:19.362 --> 00:01:25.170
The dates under each return box show the exact data window actually used.

12
00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:33.832
Above the date controls, compact warnings surface fund-closure risk and any Action Center items that need review.

13
00:01:33.832 --> 00:01:43.927
The Shared Performance Date Range then controls performance throughout the dashboard and stays synchronized with Growth, Total Return, Gains and Losses, and Holdings.

14
00:01:43.927 --> 00:01:47.877
One Day means the move since the previous close.

15
00:01:47.877 --> 00:01:51.389
Seven Days goes back exactly seven calendar days.

16
00:01:51.389 --> 00:01:57.534
One, Three, and Six Months use the same calendar day in the earlier month.

17
00:01:57.534 --> 00:02:03.240
Year to Date starts from the final close on or before January first.

18
00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:06.751
One Year and Five Years use calendar-year lookbacks.

19
00:02:06.751 --> 00:02:12.896
All begins with the portfolio's first recorded trade and runs a time-weighted tracker replay.

20
00:02:12.896 --> 00:02:19.919
Life asks a different question: current value minus cost basis for shares still held, matching Holdings.

21
00:02:19.919 --> 00:02:24.308
Custom uses the inclusive start and end dates you enter.

22
00:02:24.308 --> 00:02:31.770
Except for Life, each range ends at today's live quote when available, otherwise the most recent close.

23
00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:40.051
The NAV erosion row asks whether portfolio income has been supported by underlying value.

24
00:02:40.051 --> 00:02:50.166
Overall Verdict combines the raw NAV decline, the payout gap, benchmark-gated coverage, and relative drag into a historical risk score.

25
00:02:50.166 --> 00:02:56.741
The adjacent coverage verdict translates the benchmark-gated result into Low, Moderate, or High.

26
00:02:56.741 --> 00:03:02.304
Yield-Funding Coverage divides qualifying price-loss dollars by distributions; lower is better.

27
00:03:02.304 --> 00:03:09.384
Raw NAV Erosion, labeled e, ignores the benchmark and shows the direct principal change.

28
00:03:09.384 --> 00:03:16.971
Positive e means NAV fell, zero means it was flat, and negative means NAV rose.

29
00:03:16.971 --> 00:03:22.028
Distribution Rate, d, is cash distributions divided by starting NAV.

30
00:03:22.028 --> 00:03:27.086
Accounting Total Return, r, is the NAV change plus distributions.

31
00:03:27.086 --> 00:03:31.638
These three reconcile through e equals d minus r.

32
00:03:31.638 --> 00:03:43.270
The expandable guide immediately below explains the symbols, colors, benchmark gate, and cases where a zero coverage value can still carry a warning.

33
00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:49.392
The next strip grades the portfolio over the selected market window.

34
00:03:49.392 --> 00:03:52.972
Portfolio Grade is the composite letter and score.

35
00:03:52.972 --> 00:04:03.264
Portfolio Beta estimates sensitivity to the selected benchmark; switch between the S and P 500 and Nasdaq to see which comparison is useful.

36
00:04:03.264 --> 00:04:12.213
A beta of one moves roughly with the benchmark, below one is less sensitive, and above one is more sensitive.

37
00:04:12.213 --> 00:04:17.583
The dollar line estimates the account impact of a one-percent benchmark move.

38
00:04:17.583 --> 00:04:26.085
When sufficient transaction and daily-value history exists, Account Alpha shows the annualized return beyond what that beta would predict.

39
00:04:26.085 --> 00:04:32.349
Ulcer Index focuses on the depth and duration of drawdowns, so lower is better.

40
00:04:32.349 --> 00:04:35.482
Calmar compares annualized return with maximum drawdown.

41
00:04:35.482 --> 00:04:39.956
Omega compares gains above the threshold with losses below it.

42
00:04:39.956 --> 00:04:45.773
Sortino penalizes downside volatility, while Sharpe measures return per unit of total volatility.

43
00:04:45.773 --> 00:04:58.750
One Day and Seven Days can be too short for meaningful annualized ratios, and Life produces no grade because cost-basis gain or loss is not a daily price series.

44
00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:03.941
The remaining boxes summarize income and cash-flow behavior.

45
00:05:03.941 --> 00:05:08.930
Lifetime Income is all supported distributions recorded for the account.

46
00:05:08.930 --> 00:05:15.915
Year-to-Date Dividends and the named current-month Income box are actual payments inside those periods.

47
00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:26.392
Estimated Monthly Income is the forward annual estimate divided by twelve, and Estimated Annual Income is the full next-twelve-month run rate.

48
00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:36.371
Estimated Monthly Reinvested, Estimated Monthly Not Reinvested, and Estimated Percent Reinvested split that forward run rate according to DRIP settings.

49
00:05:36.371 --> 00:05:44.852
The three current-month reinvestment boxes perform the same split using payments actually recorded so far this month.

50
00:05:44.852 --> 00:05:56.826
Portfolio IRR is money-weighted, so it reflects the timing of deposits, withdrawals, and cash flows; Manage Exclusions can remove selected holdings from that calculation.

51
00:05:56.826 --> 00:06:01.815
Average Yield on Cost compares annual income with purchase cost.

52
00:06:01.815 --> 00:06:05.806
Current Yield compares forward income with today's value.

53
00:06:05.806 --> 00:06:13.290
The S and P 500 box supplies current index level, daily move, and year-to-date context.

54
00:06:14.490 --> 00:06:20.394
Portfolio Value Over Time turns recorded account snapshots into an equity curve.

55
00:06:20.394 --> 00:06:30.234
High, Low, and Current callouts identify the important visible points, and normal chart zooming can narrow the period under inspection.

56
00:06:30.234 --> 00:06:33.187
Daily shows every recorded trading-day value.

57
00:06:33.187 --> 00:06:45.979
Weekly keeps the last recorded value in each calendar week, and Monthly keeps the last value in each month, reducing noise without changing the underlying history.

58
00:06:45.979 --> 00:06:50.899
Price Return plots recorded portfolio value without adding dividend payments.

59
00:06:50.899 --> 00:07:03.199
Total Return adjusts earlier points for later deposits and withdrawals and includes distributions, so the rise toward today represents investment gain rather than added capital.

60
00:07:03.199 --> 00:07:09.104
Record NAV refreshes prices and dividends before saving the current account snapshot.

61
00:07:09.104 --> 00:07:14.024
Backfill History fills missing transaction-supported dates without changing recorded days.

62
00:07:14.024 --> 00:07:20.420
Repair Chart rebuilds previously backfilled points while preserving official snapshots and today's value.

63
00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:25.671
The Grade and Exposure Guide is the dashboard's built-in legend.

64
00:07:25.671 --> 00:07:32.558
It separates the market windows that can produce a grade from very short ranges and from Life.

65
00:07:32.558 --> 00:07:39.040
It also explains the beta ranges used for conservative, balanced, aggressive, and very aggressive income portfolios.

66
00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:47.952
The table lists each graded metric, what it measures, the thresholds for letter grades, and its weight in the composite Portfolio Grade.

67
00:07:47.952 --> 00:07:58.890
Use this section whenever a letter changes after switching the date range: the grade is always describing that selected stretch, not a permanent label for the account.

68
00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:03.582
Understanding Account Alpha explains the cash-flow-aware account calculation.

69
00:08:03.582 --> 00:08:13.621
The app rebuilds daily account return, removes deposits, withdrawals, and transfers, and compares the result with the benchmark the account tracks most closely.

70
00:08:13.621 --> 00:08:26.279
Positive alpha means the account earned more than its beta alone predicts; near zero means exposure explains most of the result; and negative alpha means it lagged that expectation.

71
00:08:26.279 --> 00:08:29.334
The guide also calls out the limitations.

72
00:08:29.334 --> 00:08:33.699
Short windows annualize a small sample and can swing sharply.

73
00:08:33.699 --> 00:08:41.120
The alpha card can use fewer dates than the selected range when imported transaction history begins later.

74
00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:49.413
Account Alpha is not the Alpha column for an individual holding, and it is not part of Portfolio Grade.

75
00:08:49.413 --> 00:08:55.960
If the card is unavailable, this section states which history or coverage requirement is missing.

76
00:08:57.160 --> 00:09:02.555
The weekly calendar shows expected dividend pay dates from Monday through Sunday.

77
00:09:02.555 --> 00:09:10.197
The heading gives the exact calendar-week range, and Estimated Total adds every scheduled payment in that week.

78
00:09:10.197 --> 00:09:18.289
Each day displays its own total, followed by the paying holdings, expected dollar amount, and available yield context.

79
00:09:18.289 --> 00:09:23.234
Today's column is highlighted so the schedule is easy to orient.

80
00:09:23.234 --> 00:09:28.629
Empty days remain visible, making the timing and concentration of income obvious.

81
00:09:28.629 --> 00:09:37.620
Open Month Calendar moves to the full dividend calendar when you need a wider planning horizon or more payment detail.

82
00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:43.691
The Portfolio section combines an allocation donut with a matching table.

83
00:09:43.691 --> 00:09:52.991
At the All Categories level, each color represents one category and the slice size is its share of current holdings value.

84
00:09:52.991 --> 00:09:57.419
When category targets exist, the chart also visualizes under-target space.

85
00:09:57.419 --> 00:10:02.290
The table pairs each category's current Value with the amount Invested.

86
00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:10.261
Gain can show price return only, or total return with lifetime dividends and realized gains from trimmed shares.

87
00:10:10.261 --> 00:10:12.918
Target is the desired portfolio weight.

88
00:10:12.918 --> 00:10:16.461
Allocation is the current share of holdings value.

89
00:10:16.461 --> 00:10:21.775
Diff is Allocation minus Target: positive is overweight and negative is underweight.

90
00:10:21.775 --> 00:10:28.860
The item count under each category name shows how many holdings are contributing to that row.

91
00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:34.693
Choose a Category to focus the Portfolio chart and table.

92
00:10:34.693 --> 00:10:42.570
If that category contains sub-categories, the top-level rows become those sub-categories, plus an Unassigned bucket when needed.

93
00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:49.983
The label beside the filter shows how much of the entire account the selected parent represents.

94
00:10:49.983 --> 00:10:53.690
Selecting a Sub-category drills one level deeper again.

95
00:10:53.690 --> 00:10:56.933
Clear returns directly to the all-category view.

96
00:10:56.933 --> 00:11:06.200
Because sub-categories and individual holdings do not have category-level target weights, Target and Diff appear only where they are meaningful.

97
00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:15.637
At the deepest level, the donut slices and rows represent individual holdings inside the selected category or sub-category.

98
00:11:15.637 --> 00:11:19.298
Value, Invested, and Gain now describe each position.

99
00:11:19.298 --> 00:11:28.908
Allocation remains the holding's percentage of the full portfolio, while the smaller second line shows its percentage of the selected parent.

100
00:11:28.908 --> 00:11:38.975
Switch Gain from Price Return to Total Return to add recorded distributions and realized trims; the row then identifies those included components.

101
00:11:38.975 --> 00:11:47.670
This view is useful for spotting which holdings are driving a category's size or result without leaving the dashboard.

102
00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:52.610
The final section is a detailed holdings overview.

103
00:11:52.610 --> 00:12:00.558
Value totals the open holdings currently visible and shows their cost basis; cash is not included here.

104
00:12:00.558 --> 00:12:10.376
Total Profit combines open-position price gain or loss, supported lifetime dividends, and realized trims, with the percentage measured against invested basis.

105
00:12:10.376 --> 00:12:19.259
Passive Income is the estimated next-twelve-month dividends divided by current holdings value, with the annual dollar estimate beneath it.

106
00:12:19.259 --> 00:12:22.999
Category and Sub Category filter the visible rows.

107
00:12:22.999 --> 00:12:28.142
Show Sold adds fully closed positions where a view supports them.

108
00:12:28.142 --> 00:12:34.687
Search matches ticker, security name, or category, and the clear control resets the filters.

109
00:12:34.687 --> 00:12:39.362
Field Help expands definitions for every summary card and column.

110
00:12:39.362 --> 00:12:45.440
Edit on Holdings opens the page used to change lots and DRIP settings.

111
00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:49.455
Common is the broadest table view.

112
00:12:49.455 --> 00:13:09.631
It brings together the holding name and ticker, current grade, shares, average cost, current price, category and sub-category, cost basis, current value, forward dividends, current yield, estimated yield, five-year dividend growth, Paid for Itself, Total Profit, portfolio share, and the NAV testing control.

113
00:13:09.631 --> 00:13:20.891
Paid for Itself is lifetime distributions received as a percentage of original cost; one hundred percent means distributions have returned the initial amount invested.

114
00:13:20.891 --> 00:13:27.460
Use Common when you want a balanced snapshot without choosing a specialized analysis lens.

115
00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:32.520
General concentrates on position structure and market behavior.

116
00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:35.415
Status distinguishes open and sold rows.

117
00:13:35.415 --> 00:13:41.205
Shares, category, sub-category, and Share in Portfolio describe position size and placement.

118
00:13:41.205 --> 00:13:50.855
Average Cost, Current Price, Cost Basis, and Current Value show what was paid and what the position is worth now.

119
00:13:50.855 --> 00:13:59.058
Unrealized Gain and Unrealized Percent isolate price change on shares still held, excluding dividends and realized trims.

120
00:13:59.058 --> 00:14:05.330
Beta and Alpha follow the dashboard's shared performance window for the individual security.

121
00:14:05.330 --> 00:14:14.980
The NAV column lets you keep automatic testing, force a test, skip it, or assign a more appropriate benchmark symbol.

122
00:14:16.180 --> 00:14:19.711
Dividends turns the table toward income planning.

123
00:14:19.711 --> 00:14:29.801
It retains the holding, shares, category, sub-category, and current value, then adds estimated next-twelve-month Dividends and annualized dividend per share.

124
00:14:29.801 --> 00:14:35.351
Dividend Yield shows current yield with yield on cost beneath it.

125
00:14:35.351 --> 00:14:40.396
Estimated Yield uses the forward income estimate and current value.

126
00:14:40.396 --> 00:14:45.945
Dividend Growth reports the five-year rate when source data is available.

127
00:14:45.945 --> 00:14:51.494
Paid for Itself tracks lifetime recovery of original cost through distributions.

128
00:14:51.494 --> 00:15:05.620
Next Payment, Ex-Dividend, and Frequency show when the holding is expected to pay, when eligibility is determined, and whether the cadence is weekly, monthly, quarterly, semiannual, or annual.

129
00:15:06.820 --> 00:15:10.260
Returns focuses on the pieces of profit.

130
00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:14.683
Cost Basis and Current Value frame the open position.

131
00:15:14.683 --> 00:15:17.632
Dividends Received is recorded lifetime cash.

132
00:15:17.632 --> 00:15:22.055
Paid for Itself expresses those distributions against original cost.

133
00:15:22.055 --> 00:15:30.901
Capital Gain is current value minus cost basis for open holdings, or proceeds minus cost for sold rows.

134
00:15:30.901 --> 00:15:37.782
Realized P and L is profit or loss already locked in from shares sold.

135
00:15:37.782 --> 00:15:42.205
Total Profit combines capital result, distributions, and realized trims.

136
00:15:42.205 --> 00:15:50.068
Share in Portfolio shows current weight, and NAV keeps the income-sustainability test beside the return result.

137
00:15:50.068 --> 00:15:57.440
This is the clearest view for separating price performance from cash income and completed sales.

138
00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:01.915
Every holdings view uses the same table tools.

139
00:16:01.915 --> 00:16:06.827
Click a column header to sort; click it again to reverse direction.

140
00:16:06.827 --> 00:16:09.692
Drag a header to move that column.

141
00:16:09.692 --> 00:16:15.013
Open Columns to reorder fields or hide the ones you do not need.

142
00:16:15.013 --> 00:16:24.428
The first column stays frozen for orientation when the table scrolls horizontally, and each of the four views remembers its own column layout.

143
00:16:24.428 --> 00:16:34.661
The footer totals the fields that can be meaningfully summed, such as shares, cost basis, current value, dividends, unrealized result, total profit, and dividends received.

144
00:16:34.661 --> 00:16:41.620
Filters also recalculate the summary cards and footer, so every number describes the rows currently on screen.

145
00:16:42.820 --> 00:16:56.997
That is the complete Portfolio Dashboard: headline account results, shared time frames, NAV and risk context, income tracking, account history, the weekly payment calendar, allocation drilldowns, and four customizable holding tables.

146
00:16:56.997 --> 00:17:06.601
Use the page from top to bottom for a full review, or jump directly to the section that answers today's question.

147
00:17:06.601 --> 00:17:07.515
Portfolio Tracker.

148
00:17:07.515 --> 00:17:12.089
See the whole portfolio, and understand what is driving it.

149
00:17:12.089 --> 00:17:13.918
For informational purposes only.

150
00:17:13.918 --> 00:17:15.290
